.TH NEVERPUTT 1
.SH NAME
neverputt \- three-dimensional miniature golf
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B games/neverputt
[
.B -d
.I directory
]
[
.B -h
.I hole.sol
]
[
.B -n
.I frames
]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I Neverputt
runs the miniature golf game from Neverball 1.6.0 in a rio window.
It uses the native C toolchain, TinyGL through VirtIO GPU files,
Plan 9 image and font readers, and PCM audio.
.PP
Select a course and one through four players from the menus.
Players take turns on the same machine.
Mouse movement aims and sets shot strength; button 1 advances the shot.
Escape returns to the menu or pauses play.
Enter activates the selected menu item and the arrow keys navigate menus.
While aiming, the arrow keys adjust direction and strength; Enter plays the shot.
F9 toggles the frame counter. F12 saves a PNG screenshot.
.PP
The window can be resized during play. Its contents retain their aspect ratio.
The graphics menu sets the logical resolution, background and ball shadow.
Rio controls the window and its placement.
.PP
.B -d
selects the original game data directory.
.B -h
loads a single compiled hole directly.
.B -n
exits after the specified number of displayed frames and reports the average
frame rate, including rendering, readback and window presentation.
.PP
Original maps and audio must be prepared before running the game.
In the source directory,
.B mk data
compiles missing maps and decodes Ogg audio into 44.1 kHz stereo PCM using
.IR audio (1).
This is done once; generated files remain alongside the original data.
.SH FILES
.TF /sys/games/lib/neverputt
.TP
.B /sys/games/lib/neverputt
Original data and generated maps/audio.
.TP
.B $home/lib/neverputt
Settings, log and Screenshots directory.
.SH SOURCE
.B /sys/src/games/neverputt
.SH SEE ALSO
.IR games (1),
.IR audio (1),
.IR tinygl (2),
.IR gpu (3)
.SH BUGS
Requires a VirtIO GPU with VirGL and its host-owner access.
The native port supports mouse and keyboard, English menus and a rio window;
fullscreen display modes, gamepads, VR, reflections and multisampling are
not provided. It is not a port of SDL.
